# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: lilliput-vla-param-lilliput-i-c-const-uint8_t-M-M_len
why: The reference code declares array parameters whose bound is a runtime length (e.g. 'uint8_t C[C_len]'). With a zero-length message,
why: associated data or ciphertext the bound is 0, which UBSan -fsanitize=vla-bound reports as 'variable length array bound evaluates to non-positive value 0'
why: (CI run 45581879065; C99 6.7.6.2 requires a bound > 0). An array parameter is adjusted to a pointer, so the patch declares the same
why: parameter as a pointer: the callee code, the argument values and the output are unchanged; only the bound check disappears.
file: upstream/ref/lilliput-i.c
count: 1
find:     const uint8_t M[M_len],
replace:     const uint8_t *M,
